    "body": "### Problem\n\nCurrently the list of properties includes a non-existent \"location\":\n\n```lua\nproperties = {\n  'textEdits',\n  'tooltip',\n  'location', -- doesn't exist in InlayHint\n  'command',\n},\n```\n\nThe [example](https://microsoft.github.io/language-server-protocol/specifications/lsp/3.18/specification/#inlayHint_resolve) in the specification shows it should be `label.location`.\n\nI think we should remove `location` and add `label.location`, `label.tooltip`, and `label.command`.\n\nServers might send unnecessary data otherwise, if they follow the spec and check the fields strictly, e.g. [rust-analyzer](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust-analyzer/blob/3061c4d11509546ed2250f0dda6d66aa60b0a18d/crates/ide/src/inlay_hints.rs#L396-L404)\n\n### Steps to reproduce using \"nvim --clean -u minimal_init.lua\"\n\n```lua\ncapabilities = vim.lsp.protocol.make_client_capabilities()\ncapabilities.textDocument.inlayHint.resolveSupport\n```\n\nThe problem can be seen in the source code: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/9cbb8e24c76682c4da7572377e2c20c5ab2e978d/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/protocol.lua#L363-L373\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nSends correct field names, to maybe reduce some unnecessary data.\n\nI think it should look like this:\n\n```lua\nproperties = {\n  'textEdits',\n  'tooltip',\n  'command',\n  'label.location',\n  'label.tooltip',\n  'label.command',\n},\n```\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nmaster @ 9cbb8e24c\n\n### Language server name/version\n\nany\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nlinux 7.1.3\n\n### Log file\n\n_No response_",
